---

<Base title="20. Error handling — in depth — C# vs TypeScript" description="20. Error handling — in depth: side-by-side C# and TypeScript examples." slug="errors">
  <div slot="header" id="top">
    <p><small><a href="/">C# vs TS</a> / 20. Error handling — in depth</small></p>
    <h1>20. Error handling — in depth</h1>
    <p><strong>How to read:</strong> left is C#, middle is TypeScript, right is blank Mystery (yours). Narrow screens stack.</p>
  </div>

  <section id="errors">
  
  <h2>20. Error handling — in depth</h2>
  <Compare>
    <div slot="left">
      <pre><code>try
&#123;
  var text = File.ReadAllText("data.txt");
  int n = int.Parse(text);
&#125;
catch (FileNotFoundException ex) &#123; Console.WriteLine($"missing: &#123;ex.Message&#125;"); &#125;
catch (FormatException) when (debug) &#123; throw; &#125; // filter + rethrow keeps stack
finally &#123; /* always */ &#125;

// Result-style also common now:
// OneOf&lt;User, NotFound&gt;, FluentResults, ErrorOr</code></pre>
    </div>
    <div slot="right">
      <pre><code>import &#123; readFile &#125; from "node:fs/promises";
try &#123;
  const text = await readFile("data.txt", "utf8");
  const n = Number.parseInt(text, 10);
  if (Number.isNaN(n)) throw new Error(`bad number: $&#123;text&#125;`);
&#125; catch (err) &#123;
  // err: unknown under useUnknownInCatchVariables
  if (err instanceof Error) console.log(`failed: $&#123;err.message&#125;`);
  else throw err;
&#125; finally &#123; /* always */ &#125;

// Result-style idiomatic in TS:
type Result&lt;T&gt; = &#123; ok: true; value: T &#125; | &#123; ok: false; error: string &#125;;</code></pre>
    </div>
  </Compare>
  <h3>Custom errors</h3>
  <Compare>
    <div slot="left">
      <pre><code>public class NotFoundException(string id)
  : Exception($"User &#123;id&#125; not found") &#123; public string Id =&gt; id; &#125;
throw new NotFoundException("1");</code></pre>
    </div>
    <div slot="right">
      <pre><code>export class NotFoundError extends Error &#123;
  override name = "NotFoundError";
  constructor(readonly id: string) &#123; super(`User $&#123;id&#125; not found`); &#125;
&#125;
throw new NotFoundError("1");
// instanceof works if prototype chain intact (extends Error is fine in ES2022+)</code></pre>
    </div>
  </Compare>
  <ul>
    <li>C# catches by type + <code>when</code> guards. TS has one catch — discriminate with <code>instanceof</code>.</li>
    <li>No checked exceptions in either (unlike Java). Document expected failures in XML docs / JSDoc or return <code>Result</code>.</li>
  </ul>

  </section>

